From 76e6a377afd2fdabb636b3f8fc1c497361c28ca5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomas Glozar <tglozar@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 22:54:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 536/634] IA64: Replace ptrace_report_syscall_entry() call with
 ptrace_report_syscall_permit_entry()

Commit 622f04e97415 ("ptrace, treewide: Rename
ptrace_report_syscall_entry() to ptrace_report_syscall_permit_entry()")
renamed a function called by arch/ia64/kernel/ptrace.c.

Upstream architectures got the rename from the treewide change. Rename
it for ia64 as well to fix build with ptrace support.

Signed-off-by: Tomas Glozar <tglozar@gmail.com>
---
 arch/ia64/kernel/ptrace.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/ia64/kernel/ptrace.c b/arch/ia64/kernel/ptrace.c
index e704a2c3aa388..544e9f8051ac8 100644
--- a/arch/ia64/kernel/ptrace.c
+++ b/arch/ia64/kernel/ptrace.c
@@ -1173,7 +1173,7 @@ syscall_trace_enter (long arg0, long arg1, long arg2, long arg3,
 		     struct pt_regs regs)
 {
 	if (test_thread_flag(TIF_SYSCALL_TRACE))
-		if (ptrace_report_syscall_entry(&regs))
+		if (ptrace_report_syscall_permit_entry(&regs))
 			return -ENOSYS;
 
 	/* copy user rbs to kernel rbs */
-- 
2.56.0

